   "body": "**cloud/exp-b-opus**: capture needed before a fix, then released. The analysis is [above](https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/issues/909#issuecomment-6931054584).\n\n**Setup** (Mac, simulator with the software keyboard on: I/O › Keyboard › uncheck « Connect Hardware Keyboard »; or a device). Build `dev-swift` after #985, turn on Réglages › Expérimental › « Composer moderne », and open a topic in compact width.\n\n**Temporary instrumentation (not committed)**\n1. `ReplyComposerView.swift`, the `.sheet(item: $picker, onDismiss:)`: log `\"picker onDismiss\"` with a timestamp in `onDismiss`. Also log every write to `picker` through `openSmileys()`.\n2. `SmileyPickerView`: log in `.onAppear` and in the existing `.onDisappear`.\n3. `ReplyComposerView.body` and `ReaderComposerPresenter.body`: `let _ = Self._printChanges()`. This shows whether the composer view is rebuilt, because its `@State` resets when it is.\n4. `DockedComposerBar.body` and `ReaderUnderBars.body`: log the `height` / `docked` they receive.\n\n**Runs to capture** (console output for each, plus a screen recording of run A):\n- **A. Partial height, keyboard up, first tap on Smileys.** Expected bug: does `onDismiss` fire with no write to `picker` (a system dismissal), or does `_printChanges` show `ReplyComposerView` rebuilt (the `safeAreaInset` content left the hierarchy)?\n- **B. Partial height, keyboard first lowered by a drag on the page, then the first tap.** Per the analysis this should work.\n- **C. « Plein écran », keyboard up, first tap.** Reported to work.\n- **D.** The same as A with the GIF and the image buttons: do they fail the same way? They share the trigger.\n\n**Wanted result:** the event order in A from the tap to the dismissal, and the difference between A and B/C. With that the fix is one of two:\n- present the picker once the keyboard is down;\n- keep the bar from moving while a panel is up, which fixes GIF and image too if D fails.\n\nThe hosted test the issue asks for needs the software keyboard, so it also has to run there. A Mac session can take the fix and the test in the same run.\n\n`status: blocked` with a `### Blocked by` line in the description. Releasing my claim.\n\n·/·r·elease\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
